OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F163A1786889892
OL,1,Wj5hw1~{4k7juhw1{$             G2/2
OL,2,W+.-'"-$/*%*%*%/"-$/*%Q,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GUK long range forecast
OL,4,
OL,5,COutlook for Mon 31 Aug to Mon 14 SepFAs
OL,6,Fwe move into the start of
OL,7,Fmeteorological autumn, signals for the
OL,8,Fprevailing weather patterns affecting
OL,9,Fthe UK are weak, thus something close
OL,10,Fto the climatological norm is most
OL,11,Flikely. This means a broad northwest-
OL,12,Fsoutheast split in conditions, with
OL,13,Fthe high pressure becoming centred
OL,14,Fclose to the south of the UK and more
OL,15,Fchangeable conditions developing
OL,16,Ftowards the north and northwest.
OL,17,FMeanwhile, drier, more settled weather
OL,18,Fis slightly more likely towards the
OL,19,Fsouth and east. Temperatures are
OL,20,Flikely to be above average overall.
OL,21,FThere is a chance that late season hot
OL,22,Fspells or heatwaves develop,
OL,23,QppppppppppppppppppppGSource: Met Office
OL,23,Fespecially in the south.
OL,24,ANext Page  BWeather  CReg News  FReg TV
